SOAPBOX: This was my second CQWWSSB contest, SOSB 15m, record number of contacts 1111 in the bag, way more than I'd have thought with the SFI going so low. Icom 7600 that gets blitzed by adjacent stations, 90w, inverted V antenna @ 10m.
SOAPBOX: It's a tough contest relying on others to spot you, calling for ages, you get spotted and calls come immediately. The high power stations are constantly being seen and being spotted accordingly. I'd welcome being able to spot once an hour or so, it would make a big difference IMO.
